# Project context

This repo is **personal** Lua code for [CC: Tweaked](https://tweaked.cc/) (ComputerCraft Tweaked) used **inside** the [TerraFirmaGreg Modern](https://github.com/TerraFirmaGreg-Team/Modpack-Modern/) modpack — not contribution to the modpack itself.

## Environment

- Minecraft **1.20.1**, Forge/NeoForge pack: TerraFirmaCraft + GregTech Modern (+ Create/Greate, AE2, Ad Astra, etc.)
- Runtime: computers / turtles / pocket computers from **CC: Tweaked**
- Pack may include GregTech peripherals and UTF-8 support for ComputerCraft — prefer APIs and peripherals available in TFG, not vanilla-only assumptions

## How to write code

- Target **CC: Tweaked Lua** (Lua 5.2-style subset used by CC), not general Lua/LuaJIT desktop apps
- Prefer clear, practical scripts for factory automation, monitoring, logistics, and GT/TFC integration in-world
- Keep scripts self-contained or with simple `require` modules suitable for copying onto computers in-game
- Do not treat this as pack KubeJS/config work unless the user asks
- Keep craft/transfer helpers inventory-agnostic: callers pass peripheral names (`from` / `out` / `machine`), never hard-code specific storage blocks
- Greenhouse control lives in `greenhouse.lua`; machines stay **disabled by default**
- Grow craft: `Greenhouse.pulse` (~3s on, then off) — one recipe finishes after the pulse; then poll `mv_output_bus_N`
- Lua lives under `projects/<name>/` (+ `projects/shared/`). Single-entry: `main.lua` + `<name>.cfg`. Multi-entry: `entries/*.lua`; craft fragments in `cfg/` (bundler merges to `dist/<entry>.cfg` with `[storage]` / `[recipes]`). Deploy via `python tools/bundle_project.py <project> [entry]` (or `--all`).
- `greenhouse_clean.lua` is autonomous — any computer with configs + peripheral network; not tied to `craft_ui`; keeps GH off and only empties buses
- Food always goes to `main` fridge (`tfg:ev_food_refrigerator_0`); never spill perishables into the bronze overflow crate. Only non-perishables (e.g. `firmalife:spice/basil_leaves`) use `route` → `overflow`; `greenhouse_clean` drains stray food from overflow back to fridge
- Greenhouse products are pulled from `output_bus_prefix` + circuit (default `gtceu:mv_output_bus_N`), not from the greenhouse controller block
- Fluids use `fluid_source | tagOrFluid | tank | concreteFluid` in `storage.cfg` (e.g. `#tfg:clean_water` → `gtceu:lv_super_tank_1` / `minecraft:water`); craft refuses to start if any input (item or fluid) is missing
- Processing crafts in batches (`times=N` one push); while waiting, continuously drain machine outputs so GT slots never fill/stall; sibling inputs run in parallel with a per-machine lock; UI amount ±1/±10 (1–100)
- `pizza_maintain.lua` keeps `firmalife:food/cooked_pizza` at `pizza_target` (default 16) via `craft.request`; `pizza_interval` between polls; run `bg pizza_maintain.lua`
- `machine_lock` is **in-process only** (one CC computer). `pizza_maintain` / `greenhouse_clean` / `craft_ui` / `wheat_grain` on different computers do not share locks
- Each project’s `config.lua` is **project-local**; deploy one bundled entry per computer (do not mix multiple project `config` modules on one machine)
- Shared helpers: `projects/shared/cfg_pipe.lua` (pipe cfg load), `projects/shared/net_watch.lua` (hotplug/sleep), `projects/craft/food.lua` (tag/spoil registration into `transfer`)
